    - target: {fileID: 8021706265186088782, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_AnchoredPosition.y
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8021706265186088782, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.x
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8021706265186088782, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.y
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8021706265186088782, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalEulerAnglesHint.z
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8099463261135127859, guid: a21a9ca0325425f42ae2532455c4dfb6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'William Brooks successfully defended his title yesterday following
        a demanding match that lasted well into the afternoon.

        The opening
        set was closely contested, with both players displaying remarkable patience
        and accuracy. Brooks eventually gained the advantage after a series of long
        rallies, forcing his opponent to cover nearly every corner of the court.

        Despite
        falling behind, the challenger refused to surrender and briefly threatened
        to turn the match around. Brooks remained composed, however, and secured
        the final games with a confident display of serving.

        The victory
        marks Brooks''s third consecutive championship and establishes him as one
